          "kind": "text",
          "value": "A standard bar chart retains the meaningful order of ordinal categories; a Pareto chart reorders them by frequency. A stacked bar chart can show the association of two categorical variables, and a scatter plot can show the association of two numerical variables. Many categories make a pie chart harder to compare. Therefore B and C are correct."
